          <Pad Id="rCh5u5zjYWswCidNyjoLQV" Bounds="85,810,830,274" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Clear is an optional pin of Renderer [Qt] and QtTexture: show it with the pin context menu. Off: the window or texture keeps the previous frame and the new frame is drawn over it.&#xD;&#xA;- The alpha of Clear Color is the fade strength while Clear is off: every frame the color is drawn over the previous one (premultiplied: out = color * alpha + previous * (1 - alpha)), then the elements. Alpha 1 gives the result of Clear on, alpha 0 draws no fade and keeps everything.&#xD;&#xA;- For a fade of a region or with a gradient, set the alpha of Clear Color to 0 and draw an own semi-transparent Rectangle (or a gradient) first.&#xD;&#xA;- Limits: the fade goes toward the Clear Color, not toward transparency (for that use alpha 0 and own elements). The fade speed depends on the frame rate. 8-bit targets round while fading: a faint residue of the old content stays and never disappears completely.&#xD;&#xA;- While Clear is off Qt renders every frame, also when nothing changed, so a fade goes on. Cost: one full-size texture and one extra pass, only while Clear is off.&#xD;&#xA;- Switching Clear on again, resizing the window and changing the Size of a QtTexture clear the content once.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
